//@version=5
strategy("vw-s1-q-s1k-na-modify", overlay = false)

// PROVENANCE: written 2026-11-07 for the Pine parity programme from row Q-S1k of
// docs/pine/capture-queue-2026-10-05-s1.md (part 3 of 3: an exit re-called with `stop = na` after one with a level;
// the row gives no level: 10% under the entry, far enough not to fill before the re-call on bar 53). One behaviour, no licence-held text.
// NEVER COMPILED ON TRADINGVIEW: a line that does not compile IS a reading - record the error text and the line.
// QUESTION: an all-na modify: does the waiting stop survive (it fills later) or is it cancelled?
// CAPTURE: NYSE:RDDT 1D, inputs at defaults, Strategy properties at the script's own defaults (Properties tab untouched);
// export the Strategy Tester List of trades as CSV beside the capture (the doc's header).

plot(bar_index, "A00_bar_index_CONTROL")

if bar_index == 50
    strategy.entry("L", strategy.long)
if bar_index == 51
    strategy.exit("x", "L", stop = math.round_to_mintick(strategy.position_avg_price * 0.9))
if bar_index == 53
    strategy.exit("x", "L", stop = na)
plot(strategy.position_size, "P01_position_size")
